	(text_box "Dock contacts J201 (5 V, DATA, GND), SMAJ6.0A TVS, TPS259474A eFuse -> VDOCK (UVLO 4.26 V, OVLO 5.88 V, 2.7 A)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(size 189.8 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c8e79c9a-765a-59e6-9dfe-222b9560c122")
	)
	(text_box "D201 SMAJ6.0A (Bourns): VRWM 6.0 V, VBR 6.67-7.37 V, VC 10.3 V at 38.8 A (10/1000 us); IR <= 800 uA at 6.0 V (only while docked).\nUVLO (EN/UVLO, 1.20 V rising / 1.09 V falling, SLVSFC9C EC): R201 255 k / R202 100 k: on at 1.20 x 3.55 = 4.26 V (4.20-4.34 V), off at 3.87 V.\nOVLO (1.20 V rising / 1.09 V falling): R203 390 k / R204 100 k: off at 1.20 x 4.90 = 5.88 V (5.80-5.99 V), back on below 5.34 V (dock 5 V +5 % = 5.25 V stays on).\nCurrent limit: RILM = 3334 / ILIM (Eq 7): R205 1.24 k -> 2.69 A (about +/-11 % from the EC table: 2.4-3.0 A), above the charger's 2.0 A input limit.\nSlew: CdVdt = 2000 / SR (Eq 4): C201 1.5 nF -> 1.33 V/ms; into ~66 uF on VDOCK and PMID that is 88 mA inrush.\nITIMER open = fastest overcurrent response (pin table). PG unused (open drain, left open); PGTH tied to GND [design choice: PG not used].\nTrue reverse-current blocking keeps VDOCK (and the battery behind the charger) off the 5 V contact when undocked (D-46)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 31.75 0)
		(size 189.8 17.113)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4479e10d-58a5-5496-9e67-14c3a4656d48")
	)
	(text_box "U201 BQ25887 2S boost charger: VDOCK -> VBAT_PACK, input limit 2.0 A (ILIM 562 ohm), TS window ~1-44 C, CE from main"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 235.52 25.4 0)
		(size 199.88 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e8871778-9450-5727-ad7a-394caa777fe6")
	)
	(text_box "Typical application SLUSD89B §9.2: VBUS 1 uF, PMID 2 x 22 uF (44 uF 'optimal'), L 1 uH (XAL4020-102ME: Isat 8.7 A, 14.6 mOhm max), BTST 47 nF, REGN 4.7 uF, SNS 2 x 22 uF (44 uF\nminimum), BAT 10 uF.\nILIM: IINMAX = KILIM / RILIM, KILIM = 1110 A.ohm typ: R206 562 ohm -> 1.98 A. Charge current and per-cell voltage (4.2 V) are I2C registers (firmware); defaults per datasheet.\nCD (active-high disable, 900 k internal pull-down) = CHGR_CE_N directly: low = charge (D-48 default: a docked, switched-off device still charges). R211 100 k is the contract's\ndefault resistor.\nTS window (D-48 hard stop 0-45 C): the 0-45 C window cannot be made with the RT1/RT2 pair of Eq 1-2 (RT2 comes out negative: the BQ25887 T1-T5 span is 0-60 C). Chosen: RT1 only\n(R209 10.0 k REGN->TS), RT2 not fitted. With a 10 k B25/50 = 3380 NTC: T1 (73.25 % REGN, charge suspended below) at about +1 C, T5 (34.375 %) at about 44 C; with VT and 1 %\nNTC/resistor tolerance T5 = 43.5-44.8 C, T1 = 0.5-1.9 C [CALC from the B-equation, not from the maker's R-T table: VERIFY]. Between T3 (about 31 C) and T5 the JEITA defaults\napply: 4.0 V/cell, 100 % current (REG08 reset values) - conservative.\nNTC TH201 is a board-mounted 0402 NTC placed against the cells (the pack's two NTCs belong to U101 on sheet 01): DEPARTURE, see capture notes.\nMID / CBSET: MID through 300 ohm (pin table: reverse-plug protection), CBSET through R208 100 ohm (balancing 4.2 / 100 = 42 mA, 0.18 W). Their common node BAT_MID_02 must be\nthe pack mid-point (J101 pin 3 on sheet 01); the contract has NO inter-sheet net for it (issue C-1). Without it the charger cannot regulate per cell. Until the contract adds it\nthis node is left joined only to R207 and R208.\nSTAT and PG unused (open drain, left open). PSEL = GND (adapter, 3 A class; ILIM pin sets the real limit)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 235.52 31.75 0)
		(size 199.88 32.226)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "20473165-aef8-56f5-8940-03e950a17c4f")
	)
	(text_box "Dock data (Q-47 option a, one contact, half duplex): VDOCK-powered open-drain driver, 74LVC1G17 receiver on 3V3_MAIN"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 235.486 0)
		(size 208.96 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f7b9d240-9bc7-56da-8492-4a8d42d60b97")
	)
	(text_box "Driver: DOCK_TX (3V3_MAIN UART, idle high) -> R212 100 k (R7: U203 is unpowered when undocked) -> U203 SN74LV1T04 on VDOCK (VIH 2.03 V at VCC 4.5-5 V, 5 V-tolerant input, SCLS738E) ->\nQ201 BSS138 gate -> drain pulls the DATA contact low. TX high = inverter low = Q201 off = line released (pull-up is in the dock, design §B1.4). Undocked: VDOCK = 0, U203 output low,\nR213 holds the gate low: the contact is never driven high by the device (D-46).\nReceiver: contact -> R214 100 ohm -> node DOCK_DATA -> R216 1 k -> U204 SN74LVC1G17 (Ioff, 5.5 V-tolerant input) on 3V3_MAIN -> DOCK_RX. The receiver also hears the device's own\ntransmission (half duplex). R215 100 k defines the line when undocked. D202 TPD1E10B06 ESD clamp at the contact."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 241.836 0)
		(size 208.96 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a4721bba-a3ee-52ee-a548-c50368448f72")
	)
